# UI Development Guidelines

> **Note:** This document provides comprehensive instructions for AI agents working on the React Native/Expo UI layer. Always refer to `/​.ai/​overall.mdc` for project-wide standards and conventions.

## Architecture & Project Structure

### Directory Organization

```
ui/
├── app/                    # Expo Router screens (file-based routing)
│   ├── (user)/            # Protected routes (authenticated users)
│   ├── index.tsx          # Landing/welcome screen
│   ├── onboard.tsx        # Onboarding flow
│   └── _layout.tsx        # Root layout with auth check
├── components/            # Reusable React components
├── services/              # API communication layer
├── store/                 # Zustand state management
├── types/                 # TypeScript type definitions
├── utils/                 # Utility functions and helpers
├── __tests__/             # Jest test files
└── assets/                # Images, fonts, icons
```

### Navigation (Expo Router)

* **File-based routing**: File structure in `/app` defines routes
* **Protected routes**: Use `(user)` directory for authenticated-only screens
* **Navigation**: Use `useRouter()` hook from `expo-router`
* **Deep linking**: Automatically supported by Expo Router

```typescript
import { useRouter } from 'expo-router';

function LoginScreen() {
  const router = useRouter();
  
  const handleLogin = () => {
    // After successful login
    router.replace('/home');
  };
}
```

## Component Development

### Component Structure

```typescript
import React from 'react';
import { View, Text, TouchableOpacity } from 'react-native';
import { SafeAreaView } from 'react-native-safe-area-context';

interface UserCardProps {
  userId: string;
  name: string;
  email: string;
  onPress: () => void;
}

export const UserCard: React.FC<UserCardProps> = ({ userId, name, email, onPress }) => {
  return (
    <TouchableOpacity
      testID={`user-card-${userId}`}
      onPress={onPress}
      className="bg-white rounded-lg p-4 mb-2 shadow-sm"
    >
      <Text className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900">{name}</Text>
      <Text className="text-sm text-gray-600">{email}</Text>
    </TouchableOpacity>
  );
};
```

### Naming Conventions

* **Components**: PascalCase - `UserProfile`, `CardList`, `LoginButton`
* **Functions**: camelCase - `handleSubmit`, `fetchUserData`, `validateEmail`
* **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE - `API_BASE_URL`, `MAX_RETRIES`
* **Props Interfaces**: PascalCase with `Props` suffix - `UserProfileProps`, `CardListProps`

### Component Guidelines

* **Use functional components** with TypeScript
* **Use React hooks** (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useCallback`, `useMemo`)
* **Define explicit prop types** with TypeScript interfaces
* **Add `testID` to interactive elements** for testing
* **Use `SafeAreaView`** for screens to handle notches and status bars
* **Implement error boundaries** for graceful error handling
* **Extract reusable logic** into custom hooks

